  "headline": "Temples of Medieval India",
  "short_description": "Khajuraho's UNESCO-listed temple group is famed for intricate Chandela-era stone carvings, including celebrated sculptural art.",
  "about": "Built by the Chandela dynasty between the 9th and 11th centuries, the Khajuraho Group of Monuments is renowned worldwide for its architecture and sculpture.\n\nLocated in the Bundelkhand region of northern Madhya Pradesh.\n\nA showcase of medieval Indian temple architecture, sculpture and the annual Khajuraho Dance Festival of classical Indian dance forms.\n\nTemples dedicated to both Hindu deities (Shiva, Vishnu) and Jain Tirthankaras stand within the same monument group.",
  "history": "Once the cultural capital of the Chandela Rajputs, Khajuraho's temples were largely rediscovered by a British surveyor in 1838 after centuries of relative obscurity.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Khajuraho Airport (airport)\n- Khajuraho Railway Station (railway)\n- Khajuraho Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Hindi, Bundeli, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March",
